Okay, here is a fairly comprehensive list of things in nethack 
that I would not include in a successor game due to copyright 
issues.  And yes, one can argue that this list is enough to 
fundamentally change the identity of the game.  One might even 
be right. 

I've marked with * things that are merely specific names for 
public-domain elements or old tropes I'll feel free to use.

Kudos to the Wikipedia "Mythology and Fiction in Nethack" 
article for arranging things by source; it made it quick and 
easy to compile this list. 

